T DecodedTopology                               | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 33-45     | A decoded topology, faithful to the source and repaired in no respect. vertices, reverses winding or drops a degenerate face has produced a specification that no longer describes the file the artist supplied, and `38`'s guarantee that an index means the same thing afterwards is broken before `38` has run. `VectorInterchange` takes an `OutlineSpecification` in. The codec fills it; nothing here parses.
T DecodedImage                                  | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 54-64     | A decoded image, its original retained. converted image is the defect where correcting an artist's mistake makes the image worse than the mistake did. precision loss with no origin anybody can point at afterwards.
E ComponentSlot                                 | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 72-79     | One component of an emitted image.
T EmittedImage                                  | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 86-93     | One image an emission produces — its extent, its space, and which channel occupies which component. metalness into three components is one convention among many and the consumer decides which; a wrong arrangement is a shipped asset that renders as a plausible, wrong surface.
T EmissionSpecification                         | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 103-118   | What an export produces — which channels, at what extent, in what layout, for which consumer. tiles with, and is **not** a readback of resident tiles. Residency is a display decision bounded by device memory; an export bounded by what happened to be resident is an export whose content depends on where the artist last looked. validation and its naming — the three parts that are wrong most often and cost nothing to check.
F EmissionSpecification::Validate               | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 117       | Whether the specification describes an export that can be produced at all. component, a colour-carrying channel in an image declaring no space, and a channel occupying two components anywhere in the specification it loaded second. Refused here rather than discovered by whoever ships the asset.
F ResolveName                                   | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 131       | Resolves an emission's declared naming pattern. collides with every other name that lost the same one, and the export overwrites itself.
T AssetInterchange                              | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 147-219   | Intake and emission as one contract, in both directions. occupants — this document's. ③ derives companions — `38`'s, through `34`, and where the cost lives. occupant the artist will paint on and export.
F AssetInterchange::IntakeTopology              | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 170       | Enrols one decoded topology into a topology structure, sealing it. §3 gives neither a default — and carries the structure's own refusal otherwise A scene where each occupant carries its own unit convention is a scene where `02` §3.2's rebasing is correct and the geometry still does not line up. `50` §6: a construct that will not survive is named at the moment it arrives, not at the moment it is missed — by which time the artist has already built on it.
F AssetInterchange::IntakeImage                 | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 182       | Records one decoded image's declared space, or the assumption made in its absence. the working space, and reads the channel measure from `42` at the point of use. There is no inference here from file name, channel count or encoding — and this is the document where the temptation lives, because a file called `_normal` looks like a helpful signal.
F AssetInterchange::DeclareEmission             | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 192       | Whether an emission may be started against the current document. wrong arrangement and the doubled channel are caught — before the artist has waited for an export.
F AssetInterchange::Emission                    | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 197       | The declared emission, for whoever presents it.
F AssetInterchange::Unsupported                 | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 202       | Constructs that were named at intake and will not survive an emission — `86`'s `50` §6 row.
F AssetInterchange::Report                      | Api/AssetInterchange.h           | 207       | Appends the unsupported constructs to the register, once each.
