E ShapeSource                                   | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 31-37     | Where one impression's coverage comes from — `58` §3's three sources. values it applies come from §2's channel set. A shape carrying colour would make every brush a per-channel asset, and an artist changing colour would be editing an image.
E ProfileSubject                                | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 41-48     | How the analytic profile falls from centre to edge.
E RotationSubject                               | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 52-58     | What sets one impression's rotation — `58` §3.1.
T ImpressionShape                               | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 65-72     | The coverage of one impression. input. Raw input at a low sample rate produces a tangent that jitters at every reported position, and a shaped brush then flickers along a stroke the artist drew smoothly.
E DynamicAxis                                   | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 84-92     | Which input axis a dynamic reads — `58` §4's five rows. timestamps and distance from the resampled path. The three the stylus reports may be absent, and an absent axis falls back to a declared value rather than reading as zero — a tablet reporting no tilt and a stylus held upright are different facts.
E DynamicParameter                              | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 96-103    | Which brush parameter a dynamic drives.
E ProgressionSubject                            | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 110-117   | How a dynamic moves across its declared interval. to every artist who has used a stylus, and a brush that cannot state its own progression is a brush every artist immediately abandons. `ProgressionCount` is the undeclared value and is refused.
T DynamicSpecification                          | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 123-131   | One input axis mapped onto one parameter. side; this is the document that has to act on the distinction, because the dynamic is here.
T SpacingSpecification                          | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 142-146   | How a resampled path is spaced. character. It bounds the impression count and therefore the work in `22` §2, which is why it carries a floor — a spacing declarable arbitrarily fine is a brush that can stall a stroke.
T VaryingSpecification                          | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 158-164   | What varies from impression to impression, and over what interval. varying from an unrecorded source resolves differently every time it is re-resolved, so undo and redo would produce a different stroke from the one the artist made, and `20`'s reconstruction of an evicted tile would disagree with what was on screen.
T BrushChannelValue                             | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 175-181   | One of `42`'s channels and the value the brush writes to it. §5's multi-channel stroke is one transaction because one brush wrote both channels; a brush carrying only a colour would make painting roughness a separate tool with separate presets and separate undo.
T ResolvedBrush                                 | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 192-200   | The brush's parameters resolved at one impression of a stroke. `22`, which assembles it from this plus the resampled path. Naming this the same thing would give one spelling two owners across two documents.
T ResolvedAxes                                  | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 206-216   | What the input device reported for one impression, and which of it is genuinely present. so that a dynamic can fall back rather than read a fabricated zero.
T BrushSpecification                            | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 227-326   | One brush — everything §2 declares, and nothing about which tool is active. declares what a brush *is*. A brush stored inside the tool would make brushes unshareable between documents and unsavable independently of the interface.
F BrushSpecification::DeclareShape              | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 235       | Declares the impression shape.
F BrushSpecification::DeclareExtent             | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 244       | Declares the impression extent, in domain units. It is the domain here, which is the answer that makes a stroke survive a change of working resolution; the open row stands and nothing above reads a screen extent.
F BrushSpecification::DeclareSpacing            | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 253       | Declares the spacing, bounded below by the declared floor. below its declared spacing paints a stroke the artist did not ask for and cannot account for.
F BrushSpecification::DeclareChannel            | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 260       | Declares one channel and the value written to it. declaring no space, and for a channel already declared
F BrushSpecification::DeclareDynamic            | Api/BrushSpecification.h         | 269       | Declares one dynamic. axis or parameter, and for a second dynamic on the same parameter whichever the resolution applied second would win by accident of declaration order.
