T FrustumSpace                                  | Api/CameraProjection.h           | 135-176   | The six planes `16` culls against, derived from the composed projection. inward-rounded plane culls geometry the camera can see, and the artist meets it as a surface that disappears along one edge of the display. linear form in the rebased position, and the four coefficients of that form are the plane. Deriving the planes from the eight resolved corners instead is the same answer computed less exactly and more slowly.
